Subject: [PATCH 0020] Prism: spaces dashboard as a window-level mode

Recon §8: ego's spaces dashboard is a native overlay mode of the browser
window, not a tab. SetSpacesModeActive() switches the whole window:
- the wall (PrismSpacesModeHost, overlay: a views::WebView hosting
  chrome://prism-spaces?window=1) covers the client area immediately
  (backdrop fade + overlay preload); the chrome collapse is choreographed
  ~200ms later (spaces_mode_collapse_timer_), masked by the backdrop —
  no jump cut. Toolbar row, bookmark bar, and infobars collapse via the
  layout's visibility gates once spaces_mode_chrome_collapsed_ flips;
  TopContainerView's children and the Reload menu button hide
  individually; the contents container's children hide and the active
  tab is WasHidden/WasShown (the container itself must stay visible —
  the tabbed layout CHECKs it);
- the tab strip row reduces to the mode bar: native "N Spaces ⌄" caption
  centered at tab-strip height (PrismSpacesCaptionButton, overlay) +
  the corner spaces trigger (patch 0019) — tabs and all other buttons
  hide; the caption lands ~150ms after the collapse
  (spaces_caption_timer_), in the shrink's second half;
- the wall fills the client area edge to edge, laid out in
  BrowserView::Layout at the contents top.

No dashboard tab ever exists; ⌘S / corner trigger / agent menu toggle the
mode; choosing a card or a caption item exits into that space
(focus + show completion matches the wall's own exit action).
